{"id": "Deq87xaRBPh", "title": "Video by therishikatha", "description": "Who was Shani Dev's mother? Not a metaphor: she was literally a SHADOW. 🌑 (It's in the Markandeya Purana.)\n\nSanjna, Surya's wife, couldn't bear his blaze. So she made a woman out of her own shadow, Chhaya, told her to take her place and never tell him, and left.\n\nSurya never noticed. The shadow bore him three children: Savarni Manu, Tapati (the Tapti river) and Shanaishchara… Shani Dev.\n\nShe loved her own children more. When Yama raised his foot at her, she cursed it to fall off. A mother cursing her own son? Surya saw the truth, and afraid of his curse, the shadow confessed.\n\nShanaishchara means \"the one who moves slowly\". Saturn really is the slowest planet you can see: about 30 years around the Sun, about 2.5 years in each sign. That's why Sade Sati, its passage through three signs, lasts 7.5 years.\n\nAnd every time we chant the Navagraha Stotra, we say it: \"Chhāyā-Mārtaṇḍa-sambhūtam\", born of the Shadow and the Sun. 🙏\n\nSources: Markandeya Purana (chs. 77 and 103), Vishnu Purana 3.2, the Navagraha Stotra.\n\n📚 15K FAMILY DEAL: Rishi Katha Books 1–3, ₹500 → ₹350, only till 21 Oct midnight. Comment FAMILY and we'll DM you the deal, or tap the link in bio (rishikatha.com).\n\n🌊 Do you live by the Tapti or the Yamuna? Comment your city!\nSave this for the next time someone mentions Sade Sati, and share it with the friend who fears Shani Dev 😄\nPart 3 next: the king who aimed an arrow at Shani Dev. Follow @therishikatha\n\n#ShaniDev #Shani #SadeSati #Chhaya #Surya #SuryaDev #MarkandeyaPurana #Navagraha #HinduMythology #IndianMythology #Saturn #Yamuna #Tapti #Sanatan #RishiKatha", "channel": "therishikatha", "uploader_id": "22569163881", "uploader": "Rishi Katha", "timestamp": 1792402737, "like_count": 29719, "comment_count": 95, "http_headers": {"Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "formats": [{"format_id": "dash-872479985887259a", "ext": "m4a", "tbr": 57.588, "asr": 48000, "f